# D-UMOUNT-ROOT-DENTRY-STILL-IN-USE-DEFERRED-DIR-DCACHE-SHRINK-RACE, H-DS1: the
# same-build A/B of dshrink_umount_gate on build 37897D38118AD5E2FAAC4FC (main
# tree ~/src/mxfs, 0.90.131), tests/umount_dshrink_race_ab.sh, 2/disk/caw/mpath
# on g2d (test31 test32).  The record was seen on 2/disk/caw/direct; that
# configuration's run.sh lock is held by queue kw on g2b while this one runs,
# and the race is between the module's own deferred work and the VFS teardown,
# which no attachment or transport takes part in.  Each lap: 3 rounds, the test
# hold dbg_dshrink_hold_ms=1500 set on node A in both arms, the gate 0
# (control) or 1 (fix) on node A.  prep_node.sh loads the module with
# dyndbg=+p, so A's captured kernel log of each round carries P199's
# residual-inode lines with their dshrink= field (work_busy of the inode's
# deferred shrink at xfs_kill_sb).
#
# VERDICT RULES (written before the first lap):
#   per lap   the harness's RESULT line: a round REACHES when it shows
#             P-DBG-DSHRINK-HOLD and P-DSHRINK-AT-UMOUNT; control
#             CONTROL-SHOWS-CAUSE when a reached round has 'BUG: Dentry';
#             fix PASS when a round reached and no round has 'BUG: Dentry',
#             'Busy inodes' or another WARNING/BUG/Oops line, every umount
#             and mount returned 0 inside its bound and the cold audit is
#             CLEAN; VACUOUS with no reach; FAIL otherwise.  A FAIL is
#             attributed from the round's captured kernel log before it is
#             counted against the fix.
#   SUPPORTED AND FIXED on this configuration: at least one control lap
#             CONTROL-SHOWS-CAUSE, at least two fix laps PASS, no fix lap
#             FAIL on this mechanism.
#   REFUTED   a reached fix round with 'BUG: Dentry' (the gate closed and the
#             flush done, the reference still there), or a control lap whose
#             BUG names the root while A's P199 line for ino 128 in that round
#             reads dshrink=0 (no shrink busy at the BUG).
#   WEAK      every reached control round without the BUG: the hold does not
#             reproduce the race and the fix laps judge nothing.
#
# Bound per lap, from the harness's own steps: prep 300 + srcversion reads
# 2x20 + findmnt 15 + knob set and readback 20 + 3 rounds x (mark and list 20
# + peer create 20 + list, umount, mount 4+12+30 + log capture 30 = 116) +
# counters 20 + chk_clean with alloc_witness 150 = 893 s.
893 tests/umount_dshrink_race_ab.sh dsrc1 0 3 1500 2/disk/caw/mpath g2d
893 tests/umount_dshrink_race_ab.sh dsrf1 1 3 1500 2/disk/caw/mpath g2d
893 tests/umount_dshrink_race_ab.sh dsrc2 0 3 1500 2/disk/caw/mpath g2d
893 tests/umount_dshrink_race_ab.sh dsrf2 1 3 1500 2/disk/caw/mpath g2d
893 tests/umount_dshrink_race_ab.sh dsrf3 1 3 1500 2/disk/caw/mpath g2d
